{
  "schema": "bd-mutate-spec/1",
  "_comment": "Row 175 / v3.66.1241. The band is the complete parallel-capture behavior population plus the two prior gates whose contracts changed. Re-run from a detached scratch copy: toolchain/bin/bd-mutate --spec tests/mutants/v3_66_1241_parallel_capture_services.json --work <scratch>. A separate transform control mutates M11 while running only test_transform_control_imports_live_seed_without_asserting_fixture_routing; that test ESCAPES, proving M11's CAUGHT verdict comes from the routing assertion rather than an import failure.",
  "subject": "v3.66.1241 -- simultaneous captures bind service, ports, state, readiness, seeding, teardown, and verdicts to their run instance",
  "band": [
    "tests/test_parallel_capture_services.py",
    "tests/test_v3_66_1099_capture_dirs_are_keyed_by_run.py::test_two_runs_do_not_collide",
    "tests/test_v3_66_1191_two_captures_cannot_share_a_vault.py::test_empty_singleton_lock_export_creates_and_validates_its_default_parent"
  ],
  "mutants": [
    {
      "label": "M1 the no-flag mode silently becomes parallel",
      "file": "scripts/lib/capture_instance.sh",
      "old": "  printf 'serial'\n}",
      "new": "  printf 'parallel'\n}",
      "direction": "regression",
      "catcher": "tests/test_parallel_capture_services.py::test_parallel_is_opt_in_and_the_default_stays_serial"
    },
    {
      "label": "M2 the port claim stops taking its descriptor lock",
      "file": "scripts/lib/capture_instance.sh",
      "old": "  if [ \"$after\" != \"$before\" ] || ! flock -n \"$fd\"; then",
      "new": "  if [ \"$after\" != \"$before\" ]; then",
